    <bpmn:process id="W_W1956" name="W1956. Institutional &amp; NGO Account Qualification &amp; Onboarding" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Institutional/NGO purchase inquiry
Frequency: ~10–20 new institutional accounts/year
Volume: ~50–100 active institutional accounts (schools, hospitals, churches, NGOs)
Owner: Trade Account Manager
Participants: Trade Account Manager, Credit Analyst, Sales Associate
Source: workflow W1956 — Institutional &amp; NGO Account Qualification &amp; Onboarding</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1956_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1956_Lane1" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1956_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1956_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1956_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1956_Lane2" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1956_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1956_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1956_Start4" name="Institutional/NGO purchase inquiry">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1956_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1956_Task5" name="Trade Account Manager qualifies institutional account: (a) entity type: private…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Trade Account Manager qualifies institutional account: (a) entity type: private school, private hospital, church/religious organization, NGO, foundation, cooperative, (b) collect: SEC/DSWD registration, TIN, authorized representative, billing address, (c) assess purchase potential: annual building material spend estimate
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 days/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1956_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1956_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1956_Task6" name="Credit assessment for institutional accounts: (a) unlike government accounts…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Credit assessment for institutional accounts: (a) unlike government accounts, institutional accounts require standard credit scoring per W24, (b) credit check: financial statements, trade references, bank references, (c) credit limit and terms set per standard trade account policy: Net 30 for established institutions, COD for new/risky accounts
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 1–2 days/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1956_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1956_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1956_Task7" name="Onboarding: (a) create institutional account in customer master, (b) assign…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Onboarding: (a) create institutional account in customer master, (b) assign pricing tier: institutional pricing (typically 5–10% below SRP for bulk purchases), (c) provide account credentials for BuildRight institutional ordering (if available), (d) assign dedicated Sales Associate or Trade Account Manager
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 day/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1956_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1956_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1956_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1956_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
